ProsperoSunshine: an IPv6 acceptor takes IPv4 too

A server whose address is "::" (Sunshine's address_family = both) opens an IPv6 acceptor. Linux and Windows let it take
IPv4 as well; FreeBSD, and so the PS5, keep it to IPv6 unless IPV6_V6ONLY is cleared, and the GameStream servers and the
web page would no longer have answered IPv4. The option is cleared between open and bind; a refusal is ignored and leaves
the acceptor IPv6 only (issue 64, Sunshine patch 0038).

--- a/server_http.hpp
+++ b/server_http.hpp
@@ -465,6 +465,12 @@
         else
           throw;
       }
+      if(endpoint.protocol() == asio::ip::tcp::v6()) {
+        // ProsperoSunshine: an IPv6 acceptor takes IPv4 too, as on Linux and Windows. FreeBSD, and so the PS5, keep it to
+        // IPv6 unless told, and a server bound to "::" would no longer answer IPv4. A refusal leaves it IPv6 only.
+        error_code v6_ec;
+        acceptor->set_option(asio::ip::v6_only(false), v6_ec);
+      }
       acceptor->set_option(asio::socket_base::reuse_address(config.reuse_address));
       if(config.fast_open) {
 #if defined(__linux__) && defined(TCP_FASTOPEN)
